    "result_text": "The test passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe change request \u2014 \"show me how many projects and contacts a client has\" \u2014 is implemented as a single new additive front-end file:\n\n**`src/main/frontend/features/clients/counts.slot.tsx`** \u2014 a slot contribution filling the existing `ClientDetail` region (order 5, above the projects/contacts panels).\n\nKey design decisions, following CLAUDE.md:\n\n- **Rule 3 (add UI to an existing region = one new `*.slot.tsx` file):** the client-detail route and its panels weren't touched. The counts panel is auto-discovered and registered by the slot mechanism.\n- **Rule 5 (share a KEY, don't create a new source of truth):** it reads the *same* `['projects']` and `['contacts']` query keys the sibling panels already own, filtered to the client it's handed, and derives the counts. So any project/contact write that invalidates either key refreshes these counts automatically \u2014 no extra endpoint, no state copy, no hand-maintained list.\n- Exposes the exact anchors the spec asserts: `data-testid=\"client-projects-count\"` (\u2192 `2`) and `data-testid=\"client-contacts-count\"` (\u2192 `3`).\n\nNo database migration or server change was needed: the schema (`project`, `contact` tables), the `/api/projects` and `/api/contacts` endpoints, and the `/__test__` seed support already carry this data end-to-end \u2014 the feature simply surfaces counts already flowing DB\u2192server\u2192front-end. Front-end typecheck passes and `bin/e2e` is green (1 passed).",
